    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Difference between Khadar (fertile, new alluvium) and Bhangar (older alluvium with kankar deposits) is frequently asked.",
        "Black soil develops deep cracks during dry seasons, which helps in proper soil aeration (self-ploughing nature).",
        "Laterite soil is rich in iron oxide and aluminium compounds but poor in nitrogen, phosphate, calcium, and organic matter."
      ],
